{"slug":"cli-m0-decisions","title":"Barkpark CLI — M0 contract decisions (DECIDED)","blocks":[
{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Approved at M0; binding for Wave 2+. Field names are the frozen "},{"type":"text","value":"manifest.schema.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" names."}]},
{"id":"b2","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Part A — operational decisions"},
{"id":"b3","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"A1 · ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"--dry-run","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" is client-side request-printing in v1.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Manifest "},{"type":"text","value":"dry_run","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ships "},{"type":"text","value":"false","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on every command. The CLI prints the resolved method, path ("},{"type":"text","value":"http.path_template","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" filled), headers, and body; announces \"dry-run: client-side preview only\"; exits "},{"type":"text","value":"0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Deferred: server validate-only — a "},{"type":"text","value":"dry_run: true","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" command makes the CLI send the validate-only marker instead (rule C5)."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"A2 · Dataset discovery assumes ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"production","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" default.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":":dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to "},{"type":"text","value":"production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" unless overridden by "},{"type":"text","value":"-d/--dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_DATASET","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", or the active context. No dataset listing in v1; a "},{"type":"text","value":"datasets","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" discovery surface is deferred (no server surface lists datasets today)."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"A3 · ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"whoami","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/meta","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" + manifest top-level ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"auth_tier","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"; no new endpoint.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Shows active target ("},{"type":"text","value":"base_url","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", workspace/project/dataset, "},{"type":"text","value":"⚠ PROD","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") + caller "},{"type":"text","value":"auth_tier","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from the manifest; identity/time/schema-hash from "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/meta","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Deferred: dedicated identity endpoint (both halves already exist; plan open decision #6)."}]
]},
{"id":"b4","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Part B — forward-seams (shape locked, NOT built)"},
{"id":"b5","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"B1 · Plugin ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"kind","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" taxonomy: ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"bundled | declarative | code | external","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":".","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Only "},{"type":"text","value":"bundled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ships in v1 ("},{"type":"text","value":"bulldocs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"onixedit","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"frt","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"media","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — compiled in, discovered from "},{"type":"text","value":"priv/plugins/*/plugin.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Adding a non-bundled kind is additive; command provenance ("},{"type":"text","value":"source: plugin:<name>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") stays stable."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"B2 · Registry sources = disk AND DB.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" v1 "},{"type":"text","value":"Registry.all/0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" walks disk only; the capabilities controller folds registry + "},{"type":"text","value":"collect_*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" outputs source-agnostically, so a later DB-backed install table is invisible to consumers."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"B3 · Dynamic dispatcher ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/plugins/:slug/*","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" anticipated.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" v1 compiles concrete routes at boot ("},{"type":"text","value":"Registry.collect_routes/1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); the manifest emits each flat "},{"type":"text","value":"http.path_template","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", so a runtime dispatcher is a server-side detail the CLI never sees."}]
]},
{"id":"b6","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Part C — five non-negotiable contract rules"},
{"id":"b7","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"Existence-hiding, default-deny allow-list.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"nouns[]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"commands[]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (and any enum surface) project through one default-deny allow-list keyed on caller "},{"type":"text","value":"auth_tier","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". An anonymous caller learns zero admin noun names or routes. A golden test enforces it."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"scoped_admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ≠ "},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the CLI never client-preflight-refuses it.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Only the server knows per-workspace roles ("},{"type":"text","value":"RequireWorkspaceRole","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Global tiers "},{"type":"text","value":"read","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" MAY be preflight-refused; "},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" may not."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"One error↔exit table.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" One mapping from envelope "},{"type":"text","value":"error.code","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to CLI exit code (the error-exit table); never re-derived from HTTP status."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Flat path templates; the ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_prefix","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" hint is INERT in v1.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Every "},{"type":"text","value":"http.path_template","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is FLAT and exactly what the CLI calls. The CLI does NOT prepend "},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_prefix","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — prepending "},{"type":"text","value":"/w/:ws/p/:project","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" onto a flat-only server 404/403s every core command. Prepend activates only when a server advertises the mirror ("},{"type":"text","value":"Context.ScopedMirror","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", false in v1)."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"dry_run","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is honest.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"true","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ONLY when the server genuinely supports validate-only for that command; "},{"type":"text","value":"false","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" across the board in v1 (see A1)."}]
]},
{"id":"b8","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Part D — manifest-projection rules (rescued from cli-commands-callback.md)"},
{"id":"b9","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Two wire rules from the archived "},{"type":"text","value":"cli_commands/0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" contract (§4 steps 3–4); implemented in "},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.Plugins.Capabilities","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (code-verified)."}]},
{"id":"b10","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"D1 · ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_admin","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" no-blanket-hide.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" The projection must NOT hide a "},{"type":"text","value":"scoped_admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" command from a token that "},{"type":"text","value":"might","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" hold a per-workspace role — only the server knows the role at request time; never a blanket client-side deny. As implemented: "},{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities.visible?(\"scoped_admin\", caller_tier)","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the command for any caller at global rank ≥ "},{"type":"text","value":"read","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; only "},{"type":"text","value":"none","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" callers lose it. Server-side twin of rule C2."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"D2 · Content-addressed, tier-projected ETag.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Projected "},{"type":"text","value":"commands[]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"nouns[]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" differ per tier, so the "},{"type":"text","value":"etag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is content-addressed over the projected document — admin and public manifests carry different etags (drives "},{"type":"text","value":"304","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + tier-keyed on-disk cache). As implemented: "},{"type":"text","value":"Capabilities.project/2","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" recomputes the etag over the projected map minus "},{"type":"text","value":"etag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"generated_at","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (SHA-256, first 16 hex chars, weak validator "},{"type":"text","value":"W/\"caps-<digest>\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); "},{"type":"text","value":"CapabilitiesController.index/2","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" honors "},{"type":"text","value":"If-None-Match","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (lists and "},{"type":"text","value":"*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") → "},{"type":"text","value":"304","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", empty body."}]
]},
